     "text": "I fixed the ordering in `top_words` in `textstats.py`. Words with equal counts now come out alphabetically, and the tests pass.\n\nThe sort used only the count, with `reverse=True`. I changed the sort key to `(-count, word)`, so higher counts come first and ties are broken alphabetically.\n\nI added `test_top_ties_alphabetical` to `test_textstats.py`. It checks your example: `top_words(\"pear apple pear apple fig\", 3)` returns `[(\"apple\", 2), (\"pear\", 2), (\"fig\", 1)]`. The three existing tests still pass.",
